ng important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment. "}]}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le15ob05re6aud02", "coverimg": "engenn4le15ob05re6img01.jpg", "images": []}}]}, {"id": 3, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn4le15ob05re2vid01", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "You can see the ruins of temples, statues, palaces and pottery that archaeologists found. You can also take pictures of all sorts of artifacts.These objects told archaeologists a great deal about the ancient Inca civilization.The first thing explorers found when they entered the forgotten city was an Intihuatana, or a pyramid. You can climb up part of it today, if you would like.", "id": 1, "time": "1", "image": ""}, {"text": "Priests used the flat top of the pyramid for ceremonies. You can observe the palace balconies and take pictures  of the flat rock at the top of the pyramid. Scientists think nobles watched ceremonies from a seat on their own balcony.The Inca empire started as a small group. The Incan empire later stretched the length of western South America.", "id": 2, "time": "25000", "image": ""}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John in Peru"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "An Incredible Find"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Suggestions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals like <span class=\"italic\">can, could</span> or <span class=\"italic\">should</span> to make suggestions. <br/>You use the phrase: <span class=\"italic\">You can\u2026</span> to talk about things to do on a trip.  <br/>This phrase is often used by guides when you take a tour."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can climb the steps of the temple.  <br/> You can observe the palace balconies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the base form of the verb (no \"to\").   <br/><br/>Structure: You can + verb <br/> <br/><span class=\"italic\">You can see... <br/> You can climb up...</span>"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le15ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "archaeologist "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a scientist who studies human history "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Archaeologists found ancient temples."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear on a tour of Machu Picchu."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "artifact "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a historical object made by a person "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were many artifacts found at Machu Picchu."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "statue "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a figure of a person made from stone or wood "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were many statues found at Machu Picchu."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pottery "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "plates, bowls, cups made from clay "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Archaeologists found pottery."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "explorer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who goes to a new area "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Explorers found a pyramid first."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ceremony "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a formal or religious event "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Inca used the pyramid for ceremonies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "noble "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "historically, people born into a high social rank "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The nobles watched ceremonies from their balconies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "empire "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of states or countries under one authority "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Inca empire was very big."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research an ancient site in the world."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find pictures of 6 things you can do or see there."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a sentence about each picture."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your pictures and sentences with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I use the Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find 6 pictures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a sentence for each picture."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share with my partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}